    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-2936",
      "problem": "What is the area of the square shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14195146/assets/53ab7a043ebbe03245fd0f8e1bf6438897a30d91654b6e51194205e4c302c07f.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The area of a square with sides of length $a$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = a^2.\n$$\n\nNote that each side of a grid cell measures $3\\,\\textrm{ft},$ and each side of the shaded square covers $4$ grid cells. So, the length of each side of the shaded square is\n\n$$\na = 3 \\times 4 = 12 \\, \\textrm{ft} .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the shaded square is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={a}^{2}={12}^{2}=144\\,{ft}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
